Roles and Responsibilities:
---------------------------

In a Nutrition Assistant Application, the customer refers to the end user who utilizes the application to manage their nutrition and diet. The following are the common roles and responsibilities of customers:


Registration and Profile Management:
------------------------------------

• Customers are responsible for creating an account by providing accurate and relevant information during the registration process.

• Customers need to manage their profile information by keeping personal details up to date, including:
  - Age
  - Weight
  - Height
  - Activity Level


Inputting Food Consumption:
---------------------------

• Customers are responsible for tracking and recording the food items they consume.

• Customers can search for specific food items available in the application.

• Customers should accurately record:
  - Food Item
  - Quantity
  - Serving Size


Managing Diet Plans:
--------------------

• Customers can create personalized diet plans based on:
  - Health Goals
  - Dietary Preferences

• Customers are responsible for setting:
  - Start Date
  - End Date

• Customers should monitor their adherence to diet plans and make adjustments whenever necessary.


Reviewing Nutritional Information:
----------------------------------

• Customers should review the nutritional information provided for:
  - Food Items
  - Meals
  - Diet Plans

• Customers need to understand nutritional values such as:
  - Calories
  - Carbohydrates
  - Proteins
  - Fats

• Customers should use this information to make informed dietary decisions.


Following Recommendations and Guidance:
---------------------------------------

• Customers should consider and follow the personalized recommendations provided by the application.

• Customers are encouraged to apply guidance related to:
  - Balanced Diet
  - Portion Control
  - Healthy Eating Habits

• Customers should incorporate these recommendations into their daily dietary practices.


Monitoring Progress and Reporting:
----------------------------------

• Customers should regularly monitor:
  - Nutritional Intake
  - Progress Towards Goals

• Customers can generate reports and view visualizations to better understand their dietary patterns.

• Customers should review the feedback and recommendations provided by the application and make necessary adjustments to improve their nutrition.


Summary:
--------

Customers play an active role in effectively using the Nutrition Assistant Application. By accurately recording food consumption, managing personalized diet plans, reviewing nutritional information, following recommendations, and monitoring their progress, customers can make informed decisions about their nutrition and successfully achieve their health and fitness goals.
